==column:wall==
V wide:
 F
  @
--> column_caps * top
V wide:
  =
 . .
  @
--> column_middle * top
--> column_floating * top

==column:wall==  # multiple stanzas produces multiple independent rules
V wide:
  @
 F
--> column_caps * bottom
V wide:
  @
 . .
  =
--> column_middle * bottom
--> column_floating * bottom

==railing:wall==
H: 1=stairs:90
 @1
--> stair_railing
H:
  .
 . .
  @
 . .
  .
--> railing_cap * railing_cap:180
H:
  .
 . .
  @
--> railing_cap
--> railing     # by default, models meet at integer coordinates now

==roof:room==
V wide:
 =
 .
 @
--> solid_roof
V wide:
 =
 .
 =.@
--> (multi) slant_roof          # Give gables nice flat sides
H:
 .. ..
 . r .
  r@..
 . r .
 .. ..
--> (multi) slant_roof * slant_roof:90 * slant_roof:270 + slant_roof * slant_roof:180 # highly-specific; kind of a hack?
H:
    ..
   r .
  r@r
   r .
    ..
--> (multi) slant_roof + slant_roof:90 * slant_roof:270  # double valley
H:
    ..
   r .
  r@r
   r
--> (multi) slant_roof + slant_roof:90  # valley
H:
   r
  r@r
   r
--> solid_roof
H:
   r
  r@
   r
--> slant_roof
H:
  r@
   r
--> slant_roof * slant_roof:90
H:
 r@r
--> slant_roof:90 * slant_roof:270
H:
 r@
--> slant_roof * slant_roof:90 * slant_roof:270
H:
   .
   .
 ..@..
   .
   .
--> slant_roof * slant_roof:90 * slant_roof:180 * slant_roof:270
--> solid_roof

# Currently, don't use rules for 'stairs' so that they maintain their original direction.
